## Integration with Existing Systems

### Archive system
- The Queue feature uses the existing archive functionality.
- When confirmation modal's "Archive Videos" is clicked, each watched video is archived using the same code path that the existing X-on-thumbnail archive button uses.
- Archived videos follow the existing 14-day cleanup behavior.
- `watched` and `archived` are independent flags (see the Two-Stage Status Model clarification). The existing `archiveItem()` is idempotent — archiving an already-archived video is a no-op — so the session-end archive of a video that was already archived from the thumbnail causes no problems.
- Archiving a queued video from the thumbnail X does not modify the queue entry (see Behavior & Logic § "Archiving a queued video from the thumbnail X").

### HTML escaping fix (pre-existing bug — to be fixed in Pass 1, added 2026-05-17)
The existing rendering inserts video/article titles and channel/author names into HTML without escaping (`renderVideos()` ~`index.html:1907`; Substack render ~`index.html:2114`). Titles containing `&`, `"`, `<`, or `>` (e.g. `Tips & Tricks: "5 < 10"`) break card layout and are a latent XSS risk. Pass 1 will route these strings through the existing `escapeAttr()` helper for **both** the YouTube and Substack sections. This is a small, contained change folded into Pass 1; the existing render structure is otherwise unchanged. Decision: fix both sections now rather than leave Substack broken, since it is the identical one-line-style fix.

### YouTube API
- The Queue feature does NOT make any new API calls.
- It only uses already-fetched video data (snippet, duration, thumbnail) stored from the existing fetch cycle.
- All player embedding uses the IFrame Player API, which is free and separate from the Data API quota.

### Substack section
- No changes.

### Settings modal
- No changes.

### Dark / light mode
- All new UI elements (queue icon, badge, modal, player section, queue panel, confirmation modals, undo toast) must support both themes consistently with the rest of the dashboard.

### Refresh button
- The refresh button continues to work as before.
- It should NOT clear the queue or change its state.
- Note: when refresh is clicked, archived videos are removed from the dashboard view. Watched-but-not-yet-archived videos in the queue remain accessible (this is the whole point of the two-stage model).

