## Dependencies

### Drag-and-drop: SortableJS (CDN)
The queue modal and queue panel both require drag-and-drop reordering. Use **SortableJS** loaded via CDN `<script>` tag — it handles both mouse and touch events natively, which matters since native HTML5 drag-and-drop is broken on mobile without a polyfill. No other libraries are needed; everything else is vanilla JS.

Add to `<head>`:
```html
<script src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/sortablejs@latest/Sortable.min.js"></script>
```

Initialize on each list when it is rendered (modal and panel each get their own `Sortable` instance). On the `onEnd` callback, re-sync the queue array to match the new DOM order and call `updateQueueIcons()`.

**Online assumption (decision 2026-05-17):** The dashboard's core purpose is watching YouTube, so the user is online by definition. We do NOT build offline-degradation handling around SortableJS — load it from the CDN as above. Keep only a minimal guard so a momentary CDN failure can't throw a hard error (feature-detect `window.Sortable` before initializing and skip drag wiring if it's absent). Nothing more elaborate than that.

