## Decision Log

### Session 2026-05-17 (planning only — no code written)

Decisions made in discussion, now reflected in the body of this spec:

1. **Build scope:** This round implements **Pass 1 only** (queue infrastructure, no player). Pass 2 (IFrame player + session logic) is deferred to a later session.
2. **HTML escaping bug:** A pre-existing unescaped-title bug was identified in both the YouTube and Substack renderers. It will be fixed as part of Pass 1 using the existing `escapeAttr()` helper. (See Integration § "HTML escaping fix".)
3. **Online assumption:** The dashboard is inherently online (its purpose is watching YouTube). No offline-degradation handling for SortableJS — CDN load plus a minimal feature-detect guard only. (See Dependencies.)
4. **Backup / versioning:** Git history is the backup; no separate backup file. The footer `version:` follows `<food> ver<N>`: a new food codename per major feature (number reset to `ver1`), incrementing the number for every fix/tweak/incremental push within that same feature. The Queue feature's codename is **`kebab`**; the first live push is `kebab ver1`; Pass 2 stays `kebab` and keeps incrementing. (See File Notes § "Versioning" for the full scheme.)
5. **Archiving a queued video from the thumbnail X:** Archive as normal; leave the queue entry fully untouched (still unwatched, still playable). `watched` and `archived` are independent flags that converge only at session-end; re-archiving at session-end is a harmless no-op. (See Two-Stage Status Model clarification and Behavior & Logic § "Archiving a queued video from the thumbnail X".)
6. **Queue icon on archived/grayed cards:** Stays visible and clickable so the user can still un-queue from a grayed card. (See UI Components § 1.)

**Open loose ends for next session:** none. Footer scheme confirmed — codename `kebab`, first live push = `kebab ver1` (see File Notes § "Versioning").

