- **Versioning (updated 2026-05-17):** The old "backup the file with a food-themed name" instruction referred to the pre-GitHub local-dev workflow and is now obsolete — **git history is the backup**; no separate backup file is needed. The footer **`version:`** string IS still used, so the user can visually confirm when viewing the live dashboard that they're seeing the latest deploy and not a browser-cached older copy. The format is **`<food> ver<N>`**, with this scheme:
  - The **food codename identifies a major feature.** Each new major feature (or large change) gets a brand-new food name and resets the number to `ver1`.
  - The **number increments on every subsequent push within that same feature** — bug fixes, minor tweaks, and incremental sub-pieces of the same feature all just bump `verN` (codename stays the same).
  - The Queue feature's codename is **`kebab`**. The first push of Pass 1 to the live site is **`kebab ver1`**. Any later fix or tweak → `kebab ver2`, etc. **Pass 2 (adding the player) is still part of the Queue feature**, so it stays `kebab` and simply continues incrementing (e.g. `kebab ver3`+, depending on how many fix pushes happen in between).
  - A future unrelated major feature starts a brand-new food name back at `ver1`.
  - (The prior footer was `version: bento ver3`; `bento` was the previous feature's codename.)
